    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as our clear offensive anchor. With a score of 72.41, he stands head and shoulders above the rest of the roster, benefiting from a rare dynamic platoon edge against MacKenzie Gore. While many of our hitters are fighting against the elite arm of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s favorable matchup and prime spot in the heart of the order make him the primary engine for R and RBI production today. Elsewhere, **Jacob Wilson** (51.28) and **Josh Jung** (50.77) represent our most reliable middle-infield pivots; both benefit from facing middle-of-the-road pitching, providing a solid floor of counting stats in a day otherwise defined by tough matchups.\n\nThe bottom of our lineup is currently weighed down by the difficult task of facing S\u00e1nchez, leading to marginal scores for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (42.18) and **Nasim Nunez** (40.57). We are monitoring the official lineups closely; should **Nasim Nunez** be pushed down the order, his utility diminishes further given his reliance on speed, which is neutralized by the elite pop-time behind the plate. On the bench, **Curtis Mead** was the closest to cracking the starting nine with a score of 38.03. He was ultimately squeezed out because the optimizer prioritized the existing plate appearance volume and order position of the current starters, even as **Curtis Mead**\u2019s profile theoretically matches up slightly better against high-velocity arms. We are playing a defensive game today, preserving our limited cap space and avoiding excessive exposure to high-ERA-opponents like S\u00e1nchez where the expected output doesn't clear the 40-point threshold for a meaningful contribution to our 5x5 totals.",
